wbemprox: Add MSFT_NetAdapter to root\StandardCimv2.

TurboActivate (wyDay, LimeLM) reads the network adapters of a machine through
MSFT_NetAdapter on Windows 8 and later. Wine has the root\StandardCimv2
namespace but no classes in it, so the query returns no rows and activation
fails with error 28 (TA_E_ENABLE_NETWORK_ADAPTERS). Developed for Bogren
Digital MLC S_Zero 93 and MLC S_Zero 100.

The new table lists every adapter that is not a loopback interface and reports
what the Linux host knows about it. Adapters that have a device in sysfs get a
PCI\, USB\ or SD\ PNPDeviceID built from their real hardware IDs. Adapters
without a device (bridges, veth, tunnels) get Virtual = TRUE and a ROOT\NET\
PNPDeviceID, which is how Windows reports software adapters.
PermanentAddress is the burned-in address for Wi-Fi and the current address
for other adapters, in the Windows form: 12 upper-case hex digits with no
separators.

Written with LLM assistance (Claude). WineHQ's Clean-Room Guidelines exclude
LLM-generated code, so this patch is not suitable for submission to Wine:
https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/wikis/Clean-Room-Guidelines

Base: wine-11.21 (2528aff26208257fdbf980666a4f0e66d47563ce).
License: LGPL-2.1-or-later, the licence of the file it modifies.

